# Clubbox — always-on rules

Clubbox is an unofficial Electron desktop studio for Clubhouse (personal, non-commercial). Product spec: `docs/product/PRD.md`. Acceptance criteria: `features/*.feature`. Backlog and status: `CURSOR_TASKS.md` (Status table at the top decides the order).

## Stack
Electron 44, Vite 8, TypeScript 6, vanilla DOM (no React/Vue/state library), agora-rtc-sdk-ng, Web Audio API. Tests: `npm test` (= unit + contract + Cucumber BDD). Also `npx tsc --noEmit`, `npm run lint`, `npm run build`.

## Hard rules
- Never automate reCAPTCHA. Never automate actions on the live Clubhouse service (no scripted joins, posts, follows, pings) — Community Guidelines forbid bots/scripts/browser automation. Live traffic happens only when the owner uses the app.
- **Mobile API exception (Phase 27 / 27.5):** the Electron main process may POST allow-listed endpoints to `https://www.clubhouseapi.com/api/<endpoint>`. Prefer **Token** auth when a linked mobile token exists (Task 27.5, safeStorage only); otherwise web session cookies + `X-CSRFToken` (see `docs/api/mobile-api.md`, `electron/mobileApi.cjs`). Phone SMS link is owner-approved (2026-10-12, option A) for host tools only — one-time link via app UI prompts; never log / IPC / CLI print phone numbers, SMS codes, or tokens. Do not call the mobile host for endpoints outside the allow-list / probe allow-list.
- Never ask for, print, store or commit phone numbers, SMS codes, tokens, cookies or emails. Raw captures and request logs stay local and gitignored.
- `docs/api/web-client-methods.md` is extracted from the clubhouse.com web client's own API module (`api-captures/bundle-src/`). Every row there is a DOCUMENTED body (evidence "bundle"). Using those bodies is not inventing. Do not ask the owner for a capture for anything listed there; the topic-chip, conversation menu, unread summary, replay chunk and gif questions are answered in that file, and unfollow is recorded as "not in the web client" (final). Moderation bodies are on the mobile host (above).
- Evidence policy (PRD §2): observed/bundle callable; `mobile-spike` host tools when web session linked; other community only with Experimental actions on; unsupported/in-bundle never. Never invent an endpoint that is in none of: captures, bundle call sites, community clients listed in the PRD, or the Phase 27 mobile allow-list.
- Do not edit `features/*.feature` to make a test pass. If a scenario looks wrong, stop and write the question under "Questions for the owner" at the end of `CURSOR_TASKS.md`.
- Escape every API-controlled string (the `html` tagged template in src/ui/html.ts), URLs through `safeUrl()`. Every user-facing string in `src/i18n/en.ts` and `src/i18n/tr.ts`.
- No background polling while the window is hidden > 2 min (except active_ping in a room); respect 429 backoff.
- A phase that changes UI is only done after `npm run test:e2e` passes and fresh `reports/theme/` screenshots exist for the surfaces it touched.

## Autonomous workflow (no owner involvement needed)
When the owner writes only "devam", "continue" or "go", run this workflow from step 0 without asking anything.
0. First do the "Next run" checklist at the top of `CURSOR_TASKS.md`, then tick it off there.
1. Follow the "Autonomous plan" row in the Status table; pick the first task in that order that is not done. Requirements: `docs/product/PRD.md`; architecture, API binding map and gap list G-01…G-18: `docs/product/DESIGN.md`. When a gap closes, mark its DESIGN §8 row "Closed in <commit>".
2. TDD: write the failing test or remove `@pending` from the scenario first, then implement until it passes.
3. Run `npm test`, `npx tsc --noEmit`, `npm run lint`, `npm run build`. Fix until all pass. If the same failure survives 3 attempts, record it under "Blocked" in `CURSOR_TASKS.md` and move to the next task.
4. Commit with a clear message (one commit per numbered item or scenario group). Update the Status table and the PRD catalog "Today" column.
5. Run triage (`npm run api:triage`, once Task 10.5 exists): every new live failure in the local request log becomes a failing test, then a fix, then a commit.
6. Continue with the next task. Stop only when every task in the Status table is done or blocked, or when a Hard rule would be broken.
7. At the end, write a short summary at the top of `CURSOR_TASKS.md` under "Last autonomous run": tasks done, tests count, blocked items, questions for the owner.
